      "problem": "$\\int \\frac{{x}^{5}}{\\sqrt{2-{x}^{6}}}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "Let $u=2-{x}^{6}.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-6{x}^{5}\\,⟹\\,(-\\frac{1}{6})\\text{d}u={x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nand we can solve the resulting integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{5}}{\\sqrt{2-{x}^{6}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2-{x}^{6}}}\\cdot {x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{6})\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{6}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{6}(2\\sqrt{u})+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{u}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{2-{x}^{6}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
